    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d548">

                <pb facs="0866" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3271: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Moore</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-02T10:00:00-05:00">March 2, 1929—10
                    a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Your No. 24. March 1, 4 p.m. Unless your No. 19, February 21, 4 p.m., is an
                    accurate statement of the engineers’ report which was furnished to the Chilean
                    Ambassador, please telegraph it, I have assumed that it contained all the
                    provisions on the subject of negotiation except the payment of the three and a
                    half million dollars.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
